**assistant**:
> Sure! Below are the detailed steps tailored to your specific needs:
> 
> ### 1. Create the Bash Wrapper Script
> 
> Since your program is written in Julia, you'll want to create a Bash script that runs your Julia script. 
> 
> - Create a new file called `run_combo.sh` in your `~/projects/justeco/stockings/` directory.
> 
> ```bash
> nano ~/projects/justeco/stockings/run_combo.sh
> ```
> 
> - Add the following to the script:
> 
> ```bash
> #!/bin/bash
> 
> # Define the log directory and filename
> log_directory="/Users/admin/projects/justeco/stockings/logs"
> log_filename="$(date '+%Y-%m-%d').log"
> 
> # Create the log directory if it doesn't exist
> mkdir -p "$log_directory"
> 
> # Run the Julia script and pipe output to the log file
> julia ~/projects/justeco/stockings/combo.jl >> "$log_directory/$log_filename" 2>&1
> ```
> 
> - Make it executable:
> 
> ```bash
> chmod +x ~/projects/justeco/stockings/run_combo.sh
> ```
> 
> ### 2. Create the Launch Daemon Property List (plist) File
> 
> Next, create a plist file to schedule the task.
> 
> - Create the plist file:
> 
> ```bash
> nano ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.admin.justeco.trading.plist
> ```
> 
> - Add the following content:
> 
> ```xml
> <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
> <!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
> <plist version="1.0">
> <dict>
>     <key>Label</key>
>     <string>com.admin.justeco.trading</string>
> 
>     <key>ProgramArguments</key>
>     <array>
>         <string>/Users/admin/projects/justeco/stockings/run_combo.sh</string>
>     </array>
> 
>     <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
>     <dict>
>         <key>Hour</key>
>         <integer>14</integer>
>         <key>Minute</key>
>         <integer>0</integer>
>     </dict>
> 
>     <key>StandardOutPath</key>
>     <string>/Users/admin/projects/justeco/stockings/logs/$(date '+%Y-%m-%d').log</string>
>     
>     <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
>     <string>/Users/admin/projects/justeco/stockings/logs/$(date '+%Y-%m-%d').log</string>
> 
>     <key>RunAtLoad</key>
>     <true/>
>     <key>KeepAlive</key>
>     <false/>
> </dict>
> </plist>
> ```
> 
> ### 3. Load the PLIST File
> 
> - Load the newly created plist file with the following command:
> 
> ```bash
> launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.admin.justeco.trading.plist
> ```
> 
> ### 4. Verify and Troubleshoot
> 
> - Check if your job is loaded correctly:
> 
> ```bash
> launchctl list | grep com.admin.justeco.trading
> ```
> 
> ### Summary
> 
> - **Script to Run**: `~/projects/justeco/stockings/run_combo.sh`
> - **Log Directory**: `~/projects/justeco/stockings/logs`
> - **Scheduled Time**: 2 PM every weekday
> - **Log File Naming**: Based on the date, e.g., `2023-02-10.log`
> 
> With this setup, your Julia script will run every weekday at 2 PM, and output will be logged in a dated log file inside the specified logs folder. If you ever want to edit the plist file, remember to unload it first using the `launchctl unload` command.
